## What to deliver

Build and rig the drone up operation by operation until each `parts/<part>.png`
matches the brief, the assembled `scene/` previews show the parts fitting together
correctly, and the rig is complete: a floating core with a solar-hot heart, two
counter-rotating rings, and a beam emitter projecting from the core face. **Author
the three required animations** as F-curves with the `voxel-anim` animation
subcommands: the self-playing **`ring_spin`** (the two rings counter-rotating on
their own), **`hover`** (the whole legless craft bobbing gently in place, with
weight, not a weightless slide), and **`pulse`** (the emitter nodding up and down
and settling). The animations are the fixed contract — produce all three, by those
names; the parts and joints that realize them are yours. You may add your own extra
parts, joints, or animations on top, but do not drop or contradict the three
required animations. When you are satisfied, stop: the recorded per-part logs and
`rig.json` are your finished submission.
